#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:55
msgid "Android"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:61 nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:105
msgid "Allow access to all photos"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:62
msgid ""
"When Immich asks, allow access to all photos and videos. If you pick only "
"some, the others are not saved."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:67 nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:114
msgid "Choose what to protect"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:69
msgid ""
"Tap the cloud icon at the top, then “Select”, and choose “Camera” (and any "
"other folder you want, such as WhatsApp Images)."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:76
msgid "Take Immich out of battery saving"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:78
msgid ""
"Settings → Apps → Immich → Battery → “Unrestricted”. Otherwise Android may "
"stop the backup when the screen is off."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:86
msgid "Need more space on the phone?"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:87
msgid ""
"After the backup, Immich’s “Free Up Space” removes from the phone the photos "
"already in your cloud."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:89
msgid ""
"Immich shows the list before removing anything, can keep favorites and "
"albums, and sends the photos to the phone’s trash first. Open a few of them "
"in your cloud before emptying the trash. If another service (such as Google "
"Photos) syncs this phone, removing here may remove there too."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:99
msgid "iPhone or iPad"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:107
msgid ""
"When Immich asks, allow full access. With “Limited Access”, iOS only shows "
"Immich the photos you picked, and the others are not saved."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:115
msgid ""
"Tap the cloud icon at the top, then “Select”, and choose “Recents”: it has "
"every photo on the iPhone."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:120
msgid "Let iOS continue the backup"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:122
msgid ""
"Settings → General → Background App Refresh → turn on Immich. The iPhone "
"decides when the backup runs in the background; opening Immich now and then "
"helps it keep up."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:130
msgid "Allow “Local Network”"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:132
msgid ""
"When Immich asks to find devices on your local network, tap “Allow”: that is "
"how it reaches your cloud at home."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:141
msgid "Photos in iCloud"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:143
msgid ""
"With iCloud Photos and “Optimize iPhone Storage”, Immich first downloads "
"each original from iCloud, then saves it in your cloud."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:147
msgid ""
"This uses internet data and some temporary space on the iPhone, which Immich "
"frees after each photo. For a large library, do the first backup on Wi-Fi "
"with the iPhone charging. Nothing changes in iCloud."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:155
msgid "Need more space on the iPhone?"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:156
msgid ""
"After the backup, Immich’s “Free Up Space” removes from the iPhone the "
"photos already in your cloud."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:158
msgid ""
"If you use iCloud Photos, read this first: removing a photo from the iPhone "
"also removes it from iCloud. Afterwards it exists only in your cloud (and in "
"“Recently Deleted” for 30 days). If iCloud is your backup, use “Optimize "
"iPhone Storage” instead. Immich shows the list before removing anything and "
"can keep favorites and albums."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:169
msgid "Local Network permission"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:171
msgid ""
"If the page opens in the browser but not in Immich: Settings → Privacy & "
"Security → Local Network → turn on Immich."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:184
msgid "Sign in with your own account"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:186
msgid ""
"Each person uses the email and password of their own account (created in "
"Accounts). Do not share an account: each one keeps its own photos."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:193
msgid "Turn on “Enable Backup”"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:194
msgid ""
"From then on, new photos are saved by themselves. By default, only on Wi-Fi."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:199
msgid "The first backup takes time"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:200
msgid ""
"Thousands of photos can take hours. Leave the phone on Wi-Fi and charging, "
"with Immich open."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:201
msgid ""
"Photos and videos are saved as they are, Live Photos included: nothing is "
"compressed or converted."
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:206
msgid "Backup on mobile data"
msgstr ""

#: nuvem_ruscher/core/mobile.py:207
msgid ""
"Immich saves only on Wi-Fi unless you turn on “Use cellular data” in its "
